# How to cite GEMsMAP: https://gemsmap.readthedocs.io/en/latest/reference/how-to-cite/
# Keep `version` and `date-released` in step with backend/gemsmap/__init__.py (tools/release/build.py checks the version).
# When the version is archived on Zenodo, add its DOI under `identifiers`; when the article is published, add it
# as `preferred-citation`.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GEMsMAP, please cite the version you used, and the tools it builds on (COBRApy and, when used, MetaNetX, BiGG and KEGG)."
type: software
title: "GEMsMAP: an interactive workbench for genome-scale metabolic models"
abstract: "GEMsMAP connects constraint-based computation with COBRApy, reaction and metabolite exploration, and editable metabolic maps in one application, with identity-aware pathway templates that can be applied to different genome-scale metabolic models."
authors:
  - family-names: Batista
    given-names: Bruno
version: 0.3.0b1
date-released: 2026-10-13
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/BatistaB/gemsmap"
url: "https://gemsmap.readthedocs.io/"
keywords:
  - genome-scale metabolic model
  - constraint-based modeling
  - flux balance analysis
  - COBRApy
  - metabolic maps
  - pathway visualization
